From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HFR VRR: 3D subtitle depth for each film

A 3D film's subtitles sit at the depth its disc gives them or, when it
gives none - a disc whose offsets are all zero, or a remux that names no
plane for its track - at the configured depth, which goes no further
than 10 pixels and is the same for every film. One that pops further out
of the screen than that has its subtitles inside the picture.

- CVideoSettings::m_SubtitleDepth, the playing film's change to its
  subtitles' depth in pixels, -20 to 20, 0 unless set: positive brings
  them closer. It is added after the choice between the disc's depth and
  the configured one, so it moves either.
- It is kept with the film's 3D depth in special://profile/
  stereodepth.json. A film with only a picture depth is still written as
  that number alone, as before; one with a subtitle depth too as
  {"picture": n, "subtitles": n}, which an older build reads as no depth.
- Action subtitledepth (993) opens the slider dialog for it, as
  stereodepth does for the picture, worded as its ("4 px closer");
  Player.SubtitleDepth shows it, for a button next to the subtitle
  offset in a skin's subtitle select dialog. The subtitle settings
  dialog has the same slider while a film plays in 3D. The subtitles
  move as the slider does, and the value is kept for the film when it
  stops.

Shared code: the video setting, its file, the action, the slider, the
info label and the overlay renderer's depth are generic Kodi.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
